# AMD64 thunk export spec -- shlwapi.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-15 second-game pass: DOOM's Vulkan build imports these and
# every one reported c000007b -- the loader found the native ppc64 module and
# correctly refused to splice it into a guest call, because no guest thunk
# existed.  Same class of gap as the first game, same one-line fix, which is
# the point: nothing here is per-title.
#
# vulkan-1 is the one that matters for that binary.  It renders through
# vulkan-1 -> winevulkan -> RADV with no D3D anywhere in the path, so this is
# the shortest route from a real game's draw calls to this machine's GPU.
DLL shlwapi.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# All 360 eligible exports were refused as "no declaration in any Wine header"
# -- an empty PE, and a sentinel for every import of it.  DOOM imports seven
# (PathFileExistsA, PathFindExtensionA, PathRemoveFileSpecW and friends).
# With shlwapi.h in the oracle's translation unit, 321 of the 360 resolve;
# what still refuses is genuinely unrepresentable, mostly the ShellMessageBox
# variadics and AssocCreate's int128 argument.
PROBE-EXTRA   shlwapi.h
